      "title": "1Password launches credential delegation allowing AI agents to authenticate without passwords",
      "summary": "1Password launched a feature enabling AI agents to log into personal accounts on behalf of customers without viewing the underlying passwords. The system acts as a protective layer, safeguarding private credentials while granting task-specific access.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Enables AI agents to log into personal accounts without seeing passwords.",
        "Protects private credentials while delegating login authority to external agents."
      ],
      "design_implication": "In an authentication flow, designers have traditionally assumed only a human enters credentials. Delegated agent authentication shifts that paradigm from storing secrets to managing scoped delegation grants and revocation triggers. Designers must now craft explicit delegation handshakes that show what actions agents can take on a user's behalf. Audit current login screens to introduce distinct permission gates for autonomous agents.",
