      ],
      "design_implication": "During visual asset generation, designers usually discard dozens of unpredictable outputs that ignore basic spatial balance. Separating structural layout planning from pixel generation gives generative tools predictable compositional grids. This allows teams to iterate on hierarchy before locking aesthetic details. Start designing generative asset templates with explicit bounding boxes, ensuring automated image generation respects spatial composition rules.",
